== Reception ==

Reviews of the Regera have been generally positive, with most descriptions of the driving experience being centered around the unique feel of the ''Direct-Drive'' system. [[Automobile (magazine)|''Automobile'' magazine]] writes that driving the Regera is "a new sensation, perhaps a combination of the feel you get from electric cars like the [[Tesla Model S|Model S]], which also has no conventional gearbox, and a combustion-engine vehicle with a continuously variable transmission".<ref name=automagreview>{{cite web |url=http://www.automobilemag.com/news/new-king-sweden-koenigsegg-regera/ |title=The New King of Sweden: Koenigsegg Regera Prototype Review |publisher=Automobile Magazine |first=Joakim |last=Dyredand |date=8 April 2016 |access-date=16 March 2018 |archive-date=17 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317051829/http://www.automobilemag.com/news/new-king-sweden-koenigsegg-regera/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Top Gear (magazine)|''Top Gear'']] writes that at low speeds, the noise and drive of the Regera feels like "a lazy American V8 [[muscle car]]", but that at higher speeds, the car is "instantly alert" and "corners flat and tenaciously".<ref name=tgreview/> Minor criticisms of the driving experience include the electric motor activation delay and the "slight [[Continuously variable transmission|CVT]] feel" upon sudden acceleration. However, each car's transmission feel and power delivery can be tuned to the request of the customer.<ref name=tgreview/>

The Regera's design has received acclaim from reviewers, with ''Top Gear'' remarking "there's real beauty in its long tail and taut curves".<ref name=tgreview/> Global Car Brands praised the car for differing from the common trend of hyper-aggressive fronts, instead going for a "happy looking face".<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.globalcarsbrands.com/koenigsegg-regera-review/ |title=2018 Koenigsegg Regera Review – Global Cars Brands |work=Global Car Brands |date=11 January 2018 |access-date=17 March 2018 |archive-date=17 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317035759/https://www.globalcarsbrands.com/koenigsegg-regera-review/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In particular, reviewers commend the car for its remarkable exterior paint jobs, which are described in separate reviews as being "sensational",<ref name=tgreview/> "absolutely stunning",<ref>{{cite web |url=https://newatlas.com/koenigsegg-agera-final-regera-debut/42429/ |title=Koenigsegg winds down the Agera era and begins the Regera era |publisher=New Atlas |first=Chris |last=Weiss |date=19 April 2017 |access-date=16 March 2018 |archive-date=17 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317035912/https://newatlas.com/koenigsegg-agera-final-regera-debut/42429/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and "gloriously wonderful".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-shows/geneva-auto-show/a32802/this-green-carbon-fiber-koenigsegg-regera-is-a-thing-of-beauty/|title=This Green Carbon Fiber Koenigsegg Regera Is a Thing of Beauty|publisher=Road and Track|first=Travis|last=Okulski|date=2 March 2017|access-date=16 March 2018|archive-date=17 March 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317102314/https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-shows/geneva-auto-show/a32802/this-green-carbon-fiber-koenigsegg-regera-is-a-thing-of-beauty/|url-status=live}}</ref> On the inside, Automobile magazine compliments the "well-designed" and "wildly special" interior of the car, but remarks that it may be topped by the opulence of the [[Bugatti Chiron]], a direct competitor to the Regera.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.automobilemag.com/news/hypercar-face-off-bugatti-chiron-vs-koenigsegg-regera/ |title=Hypercar Face-Off: Bugatti Chiron vs. Koenigsegg Regera |work=Automobile Magazine |date=2 March 2016 |access-date=16 March 2018 |language=en-US |archive-date=17 March 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180317050319/http://www.automobilemag.com/news/hypercar-face-off-bugatti-chiron-vs-koenigsegg-regera/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Production==
Koenigsegg originally planned to build 80 Regeras, making it the largest single-vehicle production run from the company at the time of its unveiling,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motor1.com/news/148383/koenigsegg-regera-sold-out/|title=Koenigsegg Has Sold All 80 Regera Hypercars At $1.9M A Pop|last=Padeanu|first=Adrian|date=14 June 2017|website=motor1.com|access-date=29 April 2019|archive-date=27 July 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190727072658/https://www.motor1.com/news/148383/koenigsegg-regera-sold-out/|url-status=live}}</ref> though ultimately 85 Regera were built. All sold out on 13 June 2017 to customers and dealerships, just over two years after the initial unveiling of the car in Geneva.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/new-cars/a10017484/bad-news-billionaires-the-koenigsegg-regera-is-sold-out/|title=Bad News, Billionaires: The Koenigsegg Regera Is Sold Out|last=Petrány|first=Máté|date=13 June 2017|website=Road & Track|access-date=29 April 2019|archive-date=18 November 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181118142431/https://www.roadandtrack.com/new-cars/a10017484/bad-news-billionaires-the-koenigsegg-regera-is-sold-out/|url-status=live}}</ref>
